{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0098 defines one immutable non-secret `OperationSnapshot` per operation. Today CLI and shared command-write entry points still call `emit_shadow_snapshot()`, while store/config helpers can resolve ambient state independently. The reconciler runtime already demonstrates snapshot-derived bindings; reuse that pattern.\n\nThis story cuts ordinary CLI, MCP/Python command, and store-opening operations over. LLM-specific resolution is the dependent follow-up.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Census the command/store consumers and identify the public composition boundaries for CLI, MCP, and Python.\n- Compose exactly once after input parsing and before lock/network/write, then pass focused immutable projections/context through shared command/store seams.\n- Preserve explicit-input > environment > project > user > schema precedence and independent repository-root selection from ADR 0098.\n- Add consumer-level metamorphic and effect-spy tests.\n- Remove migrated shadow calls and ambient reloads; extend the existing ownership checker with red-proven detections rather than a second registry.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py` and `src/rebar/config.py` — existing composer/projections and approved compatibility boundary.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/`, `src/rebar/_commands/`, `src/rebar/_store/`, and MCP command entry modules — compose once and thread focused context.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/` and focused config/store/CLI/MCP tests.\n- `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and its exact exception registry.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: equivalent CLI, MCP, and Python operations resolve one identical snapshot and produce existing effects. Metamorphic edge: mutate environment, selected files, and CWD after capture; the active operation remains unchanged and the next operation changes. Failure edge: malformed selected configuration causes zero lock, subprocess, network, or store effects.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Representative CLI, MCP, and Python ticket/store reads and writes each compose one snapshot/context, proven by call-count tests through production entry points.\n- [ ] Given environment/config/CWD mutation after composition, the active operation's selected tracker directory, branch, remote, push mode, and observable effects remain unchanged; a new operation observes the change.\n- [ ] Explicit operation input remains authoritative and malformed selected config fails before lock, subprocess, network, or store write.\n- [ ] Store helpers receive focused projections/context and do not call `load_config`, environment, or CWD beneath the approved boundary.\n- [ ] Migrated `emit_shadow_snapshot` calls and compatibility resolution branches are deleted, with no stored ticket/event/bridge format change.\n- [ ] The structural ownership checker catches a synthetic below-boundary ambient read and has zero new legacy exceptions.\n- [ ] Existing config, tracker layout, concurrency, CLI/MCP/library parity, lint, typecheck, and default suites pass."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788026790317907233,"uuid":"67dfc94a-4f48-4b04-b183-8b48db6df3e8"}